From my limited Valkyrie experience, I'd say somewhere between lvl 11
and 13 will be done the hard way.  My first priority is collecting
enough gain_level/gain_energy potions to alchemize a stack of heal
potions into blessed gain_ability potions.  After that, my next
priority is getting to level 14 for the quest.  If I only have 1 gain
level potion, I'll wait until level 13 to quaff it, but if I have 3,
I'll start quaffing at level 11.

Around the point that I'm reaching lvl 12, I usually have enough heal
potions to alchemize a large stack of blessed gain ability so that I
can safely play with foocubi.  It's also around the point where
leveling up through killing monsters becomes a lot more annoying than
finding foocubi without headaches.

The continued exponential rise in XP necessary to level up certainly
seems like a questionable decision by the dev team, since XP earned
becomes completely irrelevant to me after level 13 or so.


